Implementation Plan: Production VM Caching Strategy
Overview
Consolidate VM data fetching across the app into a single unified hook with production-ready caching. Currently, Virtual Machines, Infrastructure, and Recovery Applications each fetch or depend on separate VM data sources with inconsistent stale times. This creates performance issues (unnecessary refetches) and potential data divergence. We'll create a unified useVirtualMachines() hook that all features depend on, with consistent 15-minute stale time, proper error handling, and documented invalidation strategy.

Architecture Decisions
Single source of truth: Create useVirtualMachines() hook that combines VM list + topology into one cached query
Consistent stale time: 15 minutes across all VM data (VMs page uses this already)
Query deduplication: React Query automatically dedupes multiple consumers of the same queryKey
Gradual migration: Keep old hooks as thin wrappers during transition, then remove
Backward compatible: No component changes until new hook is proven working
